The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```text
if (is_compressed(ni)) {
	ni_lock(ni);
	err = ni_read_folio_cmpr(ni, folio);
	ni_unlock(ni);
	return err;
}
```
Reason:
This code acquires `ni_lock` before calling `ni_read_folio_cmpr`. Inside `ni_read_folio_cmpr`, the function attempts to lock all pages in the compressed frame. This creates a lock ordering of `ni_lock` → page lock, which violates the VFS‑enforced order (page lock before filesystem lock). When another task (e.g., readahead) already holds the page lock and tries to acquire `ni_lock`, a deadlock occurs.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```text
if (is_compressed(ni)) {
	/* ni_lock is taken inside ni_read_folio_cmpr after page locks */
	err = ni_read_folio_cmpr(ni, folio);
	return err;
}
```
Reason:
Removing the `ni_lock`/`ni_unlock` pair from `ntfs_read_folio` ensures that the filesystem lock is not held when entering `ni_read_folio_cmpr`. The fix further requires that `ni_read_folio_cmpr` acquires `ni_lock` only after all page locks in the compressed frame have been successfully obtained. This restores the correct lock ordering (page lock → `ni_lock`), eliminating the deadlock.

